WEBVTT

00:03.090 --> 00:06.290
Woof, woof.

00:08.090 --> 00:10.690
Is it... a dog?

00:10.690 --> 00:11.960
That's right!

01:43.770 --> 01:45.160
Thanks for waiting.

01:45.560 --> 01:47.260
Who ordered the "A" lunch combo?

01:47.660 --> 01:48.540
That would be us.

01:50.500 --> 01:52.500
What the, why don't I get a salad?

01:52.500 --> 01:55.730
Why do you guys get one and I don't?

01:59.490 --> 02:02.150
I don't think you ordered a lunch combo, Antkiller.

02:02.150 --> 02:04.820
Entrées don't come with a salad, I think.

02:04.820 --> 02:07.120
"Don't come with a salad, I think?"

02:07.120 --> 02:08.790
You should have told me sooner!

02:08.790 --> 02:10.760
I want a salad too, you know.

02:10.760 --> 02:13.210
I haven't been eating many vegetables lately.

02:13.210 --> 02:15.490
In that case, I'll have them change your order to a lunch combo too!

02:17.480 --> 02:22.450
Anyway, don't you guys think my orders to eliminate Sunred are way overdue?

02:23.110 --> 02:24.180
Yeah.

02:24.180 --> 02:25.380
To be honest,

02:25.380 --> 02:27.230
you're at least a hundred times stronger than Gadgem,

02:27.230 --> 02:29.920
who's also a sand monster.

02:29.920 --> 02:33.120
Stop exaggerating, dumbass.

02:33.120 --> 02:34.930
You got the strong part right, though.

02:34.930 --> 02:38.820
They really should have sent you to kill Sunred before all those guys.

02:39.710 --> 02:44.010
I didn't mind that Gadgem got to fight first since he's got seniority and everything,

02:44.010 --> 02:48.380
but I really don't get why Mosqui got to fight before I did.

02:48.380 --> 02:49.450
Yeah, for sure.

02:49.450 --> 02:52.570
I'm sure things went down that way because of the operational circumstances back then.

02:52.570 --> 02:56.220
Well I'm not a kid, so it's not like I'm going to go bitch at Master Vamp.

02:56.220 --> 03:01.930
But since I did get picked this time, I'll make sure Red gets a glimpse of hell.

03:02.130 --> 03:05.610
I've been certified for a murder license, after all.

03:07.480 --> 03:09.090
A murder license, huh?

03:09.590 --> 03:11.490
But I have to tell you,

03:11.490 --> 03:13.840
Red is unbelievably strong.

03:13.840 --> 03:14.440
Ow!

03:15.100 --> 03:16.240
So?

03:16.240 --> 03:19.980
Do you think that matters to me?

03:19.980 --> 03:20.150
Sorry.

03:20.150 --> 03:23.180
I'm 200% sure that I'm going to beat his ass.

03:23.180 --> 03:24.340
200%

03:24.340 --> 03:26.730
Once I drag Red into my sandpit trap

03:26.730 --> 03:29.560
and bury him in the sand, he won't even be able to land a kick.

03:29.560 --> 03:31.740
Because he can't use his full strength, even his punches will only be about half power.

03:31.740 --> 03:35.500
In the meantime, I'll be making the most out of my home court advantage in the sand.

03:35.500 --> 03:39.020
I'm actually wondering if it's even possible to lose!

03:39.020 --> 03:40.090
That's right.

03:40.090 --> 03:44.410
We should go show Red that it's impossible for you to lose!

03:42.790 --> 03:45.710
Yeah, we'll show him!

03:44.410 --> 03:47.780
By the way, are you guys doing anything after this?

03:48.080 --> 03:50.490
Not really.

03:50.490 --> 03:52.240
Then you guys should tag along.

03:52.240 --> 03:55.930
I'm going to go look for a place where I can set up my sandpit trap.

03:57.750 --> 03:59.950
There's more gravel here than I thought.

03:59.950 --> 04:02.780
It's not grainy because of all the moisture around too.

04:04.180 --> 04:07.340
I guess parks weren't meant for sandpit traps either.

04:07.340 --> 04:11.360
They usually use sticky soil to minimize the dust.

04:11.360 --> 04:12.790
It's like that here too.

04:13.710 --> 04:16.240
They paved most of the roads around here,

04:16.240 --> 04:19.120
so it's hard to find soil in this area.

04:19.120 --> 04:23.080
The world's become such a difficult place to live in.

04:30.190 --> 04:33.800
We found a place for your sandpit trap, Antkiller.

04:33.800 --> 04:34.870
Really?

04:34.870 --> 04:37.450
You know where the orthopedic clinic across the railroad tracks is, right?

04:37.450 --> 04:40.160
There's a house over there, owned by Mr. Shibata.

04:40.160 --> 04:42.780
Apparently there's land available inside the yard.

04:44.720 --> 04:46.050
Right here.

04:46.050 --> 04:50.830
They're not planting anything this year because they were planning to renovate or something.

04:51.130 --> 04:52.440
They <i>were</i> planning?

04:52.740 --> 04:56.620
Yeah, Mr. Shibata apparently called it off after arguing with his son about it.

04:57.420 --> 05:00.070
But is it really okay for us to use this land?

05:00.070 --> 05:03.800
Mr. Shibata said we could, so we should take him up on his offer.

05:03.800 --> 05:06.890
I'll bring him some salad oil to show our appreciation later.

05:06.890 --> 05:08.470
O-Okay then.

05:12.940 --> 05:14.370
Is it done?

05:14.370 --> 05:16.500
Yeah, this is basically it.

05:17.300 --> 05:18.880
Why, hello there.

05:18.880 --> 05:21.450
Thank you for letting us use your land, Mr. Shibata.

05:21.450 --> 05:22.600
Thank you so much.

05:23.770 --> 05:25.930
So this is the sandpit trap I heard about.

05:25.930 --> 05:27.210
It's very beautiful.

05:27.210 --> 05:27.810
Isn't it?

05:27.810 --> 05:31.050
You shouldn't get too close, since bad things will happen if you fall in.

05:31.050 --> 05:33.180
How was the soil?

05:33.180 --> 05:34.970
It was just right.

05:34.970 --> 05:36.790
This land was converted from sand,

05:36.790 --> 05:39.500
so the most we can ever grow here are potatoes and such.

05:39.500 --> 05:43.320
Actually, the graininess of the soil here makes it ideal for sandpit traps,

05:43.320 --> 05:46.240
so I'm sure even Red won't be able to get out if he were to fall in.

05:46.240 --> 05:47.080
Pops.

05:49.170 --> 05:51.020
Shigehiko!

05:51.020 --> 05:52.840
What are you doing here?

05:53.440 --> 05:58.410
I was wondering if we could go over the blueprints for the house with Mr. Tomita one more time.

05:59.670 --> 06:02.790
I really should have listened to you.

06:02.790 --> 06:05.040
When I heard you asked Mr. Tomita to draw the blueprints,

06:05.040 --> 06:07.930
I thought you were just trying to push your agenda again.

06:08.230 --> 06:11.710
But Mom sent the blueprints over by fax,

06:11.710 --> 06:14.270
and I found out that everything was just the way I wanted, right down to the kitchen.

06:14.870 --> 06:17.200
Well I did some rethinking,

06:17.200 --> 06:23.010
and I figured I should respect your opinions since you're going to be living there longer.

06:23.410 --> 06:24.210
Thanks, pops.

06:24.210 --> 06:25.210
Oh, I know.

06:25.210 --> 06:28.840
Why don't we give Mr. Tomita a call right now.

06:29.910 --> 06:31.560
Oh, don't worry about a thing.

06:31.560 --> 06:34.850
You'll still have time to have your fight here.

06:35.450 --> 06:39.740
In that case, we'll bring Mr. Red out here and get him into the sandpit trap right away.

06:39.740 --> 06:41.800
Please do.

06:43.580 --> 06:45.480
Aren't you glad that Mr. Shibata's getting along with his son again?

06:45.480 --> 06:47.690
Yeah, it's such a nice story.

06:47.690 --> 06:48.940
It sure is.

06:54.000 --> 06:55.660
It's gotta be an accident!

06:55.660 --> 06:57.860
I mean who'd have thought that he'd get to you before the trap was ready?

06:57.860 --> 06:59.570
Yeah, it's gotta be an accident.

06:59.570 --> 07:00.970
You would have had him if he had fallen for the trap.

07:00.970 --> 07:04.950
Who the hell just shows up out of the blue like that?

07:04.950 --> 07:07.310
Now he's got me all pissed.

07:07.310 --> 07:09.590
Next time he won't get off easy.

07:09.590 --> 07:11.570
I swear it.

07:11.570 --> 07:13.240
Well, hear me out...

07:18.590 --> 07:22.020
Sukiyaki-cut beef sirloin,

07:22.020 --> 07:25.020
2 dollars 38 cents for 100 grams!

07:25.020 --> 07:28.490
I got a good deal because of the leftover sale.

07:28.490 --> 07:31.500
I guess I should feed <i>that</i>  something good from time to time.

07:34.850 --> 07:35.900
Isn't this...

07:39.390 --> 07:41.490
Damn it, I lost again.

07:41.490 --> 07:45.800
If it weren't for those punks, I would have gotten there on time and have gotten a good seat.

07:45.800 --> 07:47.210
Please, stop.

07:47.210 --> 07:49.980
You're touching my weak spot over there.

07:49.980 --> 07:51.780
Come on, hold it in for a while.

07:51.780 --> 07:52.690
Just hold still-

07:52.690 --> 07:53.860
K-Kayoko, are you...?

07:54.310 --> 07:55.440
Red!

07:55.440 --> 07:57.830
How dare you set foot in this house again, you-

07:59.380 --> 08:01.060
What the hell are you doing?

08:01.060 --> 08:02.210
I'm disappointed in you!

08:02.210 --> 08:02.890
The hell?

08:02.890 --> 08:03.910
Stop playing dumb!

08:03.910 --> 08:06.180
I know you're the one who did this to Usa.

08:06.180 --> 08:08.830
Don't tell me you'd go all out on a cute thing like Usa too.

08:08.830 --> 08:10.280
It wasn't me!

08:10.280 --> 08:12.190
He did this to himself.

08:12.190 --> 08:14.690
But isn't he from Vamp's place?

08:14.690 --> 08:16.570
Who else would do this to him besides you?

08:16.570 --> 08:19.760
Like I said it wasn't... just hear me out, okay?

08:21.520 --> 08:24.430
I was passing through the area in front of the park on my way to pachinko.

08:24.430 --> 08:25.220
He's here.

08:27.790 --> 08:29.010
Now, P-chan!

08:43.630 --> 08:45.310
He got us.

08:45.710 --> 08:47.500
Holy crap that was close.

08:47.500 --> 08:50.010
That was the most dangerous attempt out of all the times you guys tried.

08:51.080 --> 08:53.340
Hey, you still alive?

08:53.340 --> 08:54.870
Y-Yeah.

08:54.870 --> 08:56.190
Is he okay?

08:57.700 --> 08:59.330
Charging in progress.

08:59.330 --> 09:02.910
8 hours and 35 minutes until reboot.

09:04.330 --> 09:06.340
I've got somewhere to be so I'm leaving, okay?

09:06.640 --> 09:07.530
Sure.

09:07.530 --> 09:08.300
See ya.

09:10.140 --> 09:11.840
Is that true, Usa?

09:11.840 --> 09:12.950
Y-Yeah.

09:12.950 --> 09:16.070
You need to explain things better, you punk!

09:16.070 --> 09:17.440
Stop that!

09:18.240 --> 09:19.440
Listen, Usa.

09:19.440 --> 09:23.130
You need to leave the killing of this guy to the big scary monsters,

09:23.130 --> 09:25.430
and not go overboard like you did this time.

09:25.930 --> 09:27.030
Okay?

09:27.030 --> 09:29.000
S-Sure.

09:29.000 --> 09:30.370
What the hell are they saying?

09:30.370 --> 09:31.800
You're such a good boy.

09:32.400 --> 09:34.310
But I've got to say,

09:34.310 --> 09:36.940
your sewing's never going to get better, is it.

09:36.940 --> 09:39.420
At least try to use matching color thread.

09:39.420 --> 09:40.640
Well sor-ry!

09:40.640 --> 09:43.460
Come on Usako, I'll patch you up nice and new.

09:44.060 --> 09:46.070
He's been living by himself for quite a bit,

09:46.070 --> 09:47.490
so he's really good at sewing.

09:47.490 --> 09:48.910
Thanks for announcing it to the world.

09:48.910 --> 09:50.760
Come on, I'll patch you up.

09:50.760 --> 09:52.650
N-No!

09:52.650 --> 09:53.680
Ow!

09:53.680 --> 09:55.710
You punk, what the hell was that for?

09:55.710 --> 09:56.570
Usa!

09:56.770 --> 09:59.950
I'll get you next time, Red!

10:01.220 --> 10:02.990
Damn it, what's up with that punk.

10:02.990 --> 10:05.350
Are you okay?

10:06.360 --> 10:08.070
Usa...

10:10.180 --> 10:13.450
Thank god you're okay, Usa.

10:13.450 --> 10:17.580
You were already gone when I was cleaning myself with the water at the park.

10:15.260 --> 10:19.360
Charging is almost complete.

10:17.580 --> 10:19.360
You don't have to worry about me, Devilcat.

10:19.360 --> 10:22.610
I would've never imagined Kayoko would be the one to pick you up.

10:22.610 --> 10:24.360
I better go thank her later.

10:24.360 --> 10:27.360
Weren't you worried as well, Master Vamp?

10:25.160 --> 10:27.360
Charging complete.

10:27.360 --> 10:31.110
I like that you guys are all so gung-ho about taking Mr. Red down,

10:27.460 --> 10:31.110
Booting... Loading data from memory.

10:31.110 --> 10:33.380
but you guys really should let me know before you try something like this.

10:33.980 --> 10:35.420
We're sorry.

10:35.420 --> 10:37.300
I'll let you guys off this time.

10:37.700 --> 10:41.490
But I guess Kayoko's not all that great at sewing.

10:41.890 --> 10:45.290
Come here Usakotsu. I'll patch you up.

10:48.640 --> 10:51.240
Looks like my eyes have gotten worse lately.

10:51.340 --> 10:53.950
Um, Master Vamp?

10:53.950 --> 10:57.110
I think I'd rather stay like this for the time being.

10:57.310 --> 10:58.390
Huh, what?

11:01.420 --> 11:03.970
I wonder if Usa's okay.

11:03.970 --> 11:06.410
Can't you think about anything else?

11:06.410 --> 11:08.320
But he's a stuffed animal,

11:08.320 --> 11:10.560
he moves and speaks!

11:10.560 --> 11:12.100
Oh come on.

11:14.200 --> 11:15.540
I see now.

11:16.040 --> 11:17.910
You're jealous, aren't you?

11:17.910 --> 11:19.110
In your dreams.

11:23.140 --> 11:24.750
Kayoko...

11:25.150 --> 11:26.990
Astro Fighter Sunred.

11:26.990 --> 11:29.750
This is the magnificent story of the conflict between good and evil

11:29.750 --> 11:33.070
that takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
